 "text": "What if everyone on Earth woke up 10% Nigerian? Not on paper, in the blood. Here's what would actually happen. Day 1. Every DNA test on the planet comes back the same. Nigeria. 8.2 billion people with Nigerian roots? Yesterday, it was 237 million. Day 2. The people who hated us are us now. Hate forums go quiet overnight. Family group chats get louder, and somebody's uncle forwards the same voice note to 40 people. Day 3. Every parent on Earth asks the same question at the same time. Why are you not a doctor yet? In Oslo, a 9-year-old gets the speech over a B+. Week 1. Everyone wants the green passport. The embassy queues wrap around the block. At the window, the answer is short. You need a Nigerian parent, and 10% doesn't count. Week 2. Joliff Wars go global. London hosts a cook-off with 4,000 people. Nigeria wins. Ghana says theirs is still better. Month 1. Afro beats is just called music now. People already found Nigerian artists over 1 billion times on Spotify last year. This year, your grandmother knows the dance. Year 1. Money flows to Lagos. The diaspora already sends home $21 billion a year. Now, everybody has an auntie in Lagos asking them to send something small. 10 years later, racism doesn't survive the family reunion. It's hard to hate people you share Jolof with every Sunday. So, what's the first thing you'd do as a 10% Nigerian? Follow for part 2."
